    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Ben Folds Five’s self-titled debut is a sharp, piano-driven alt-rock record that helped define the band’s off-kilter, hook-heavy identity. Released in 1995, it pairs Ben Folds’ sardonic songwriting and melodic gift with a rhythm section that gives songs like “Underground,” “Philosophy,” and “Jackson Cannery” their brash momentum, balancing humor, angst, and tightly wound musicianship.\n\nThe 30th Anniversary edition expands that original album with a newly remastered version and a bonus disc featuring the long-rumored “Shelved First Attempt,” an earlier abandoned version of the record. That extra material includes alternate takes and unreleased songs, giving a fuller picture of how the album took shape and underscoring its lasting importance as one of the era’s more distinctive rock debuts.",
